{"name":"Rucksack Tan","hex":"#edb508","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rucksack","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bag carried on the back or shoulder, supported by straps."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rucksack"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Backpack","blocks":[{"text":"A backpack, also called knapsack, schoolbag, rucksack, pack, booksack, bookbag, haversack, packsack, or backsack, is in its simplest frameless form, a fabric sack carried on one’s back and secured with two straps that go over the shoulders, and is used to carry goods from one place to another. It can feature an external or internal frame to transfer heavy loads off the user’s shoulders and onto their hips, reducing strain and increasing comfort on long hikes with heavy gear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Rucksack1.jpg/330px-Rucksack1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backpack"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Canon-Deluxe_Backpack-200-EG.jpg/500px-Canon-Deluxe_Backpack-200-EG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Canon-Deluxe_Backpack-200-EG.jpg/1280px-Canon-Deluxe_Backpack-200-EG.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki